WEBVTT

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.270
F-Found him!

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.070
Hey boy!

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.450
Caster?

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.670
There's something I'd like you to teach me!

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:45.580
Excuse me?

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:57.240
What a lovely day to hang the wash!

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.120
Honestly, I can't thank you enough

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.700
for sparring with me again today, Mr. Souichirou.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:02.790
Oh no.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.210
I'd be happy to spar with you anytime.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:09.210
Thanks to you, I'm sure I'll be
able to savor tonight's dinner.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.130
Master Souichirou!

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:13.210
Come to think of it, last night's taro simmered in broth...

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:16.840
The flavors were so well-steeped. It was truly delicious!

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:20.140
Mr. Souichirou, you should
have Medea make it for you, too.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.760
Perhaps.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.560
Taro simmered in broth?

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.940
H-How would you make that?

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.650
Boil the taro

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.690
and roll them around?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.150
I have no clue!

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.370
But if Master Souichirou wishes to eat it...

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:03.430
Well, well, here comes an odd couple!

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.980
Who's that? Your young gigolo?

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.110
Whatever. Just give me some mackerel pike, will you?

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.270
Sure thing!

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.190
And how about your friend?

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.780
Oh, she says she's training to cook.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.990
You? Cook? You serious?

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.780
You've got to be kidding me!

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.490
I'll burn you up, you cur.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.250
Hey, hey!

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:28.540
Here! Your mackerel pike.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:29.830
Thanks.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.540
For Master Souichirou's sake, I shall do my best!

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.260
Someone's enjoying being a newlywed!

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:45.060
Just as expected, everything's immaculate!

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.720
But really, I'm indebted to you!

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.520
Thanks to you,

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.350
I can serve Master Souichirou taro
simmered in broth I've prepared myself.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.360
Now then, boy, please get started.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.070
<i>Wow, she's totally into her role as wife!</i>

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.080
All right, then, let's get started!

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.870
At your request, Caster, taro simmered in broth,

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:11.330
marinated mustard spinach and miso soup...

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.250
The main dish will be mackerel
pike which is in season now.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.380
It's fatty, and it's gonna taste great!

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:19.340
So balance is important when it comes to meals.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.340
I'd like you to teach me about that, too.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:25.010
We're gonna start by peeling the taro.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.510
When they're freshly-harvested,

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.480
you can remove the peel just
by rubbing them with a cloth.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.190
But today's aren't so new,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.270
so peel them pretty thick after
chopping off the tops and bottoms.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:43.410
You're so proficient.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.370
Didn't I ever tell you?

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:50.200
I use knives for my magic spells.
I'm quite used to handling them.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:57.040
To remove the sliminess from the
taro, we're going to parboil them.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:01.130
Add the taro to boiling water,
simmer for three to four minutes,

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:05.890
then run them under cold water
as you wash away the sliminess.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:12.690
Place the taro and enough broth to
cover them in a pot, and turn on the heat.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:17.770
When it comes to a boil,
add sugar, sake and sweet rice wine,

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.190
cover it all with a drop-lid,

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.650
and cook over low heat for five
to six minutes until it starts to boil.

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.660
Add soy sauce. Then, boil it down
for another five to six minutes.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:33.960
When there's only a little broth left,
shake the pot so that it doesn't burn.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.170
Mix the broth and taro together,

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.380
and once the taro turn glossy, they're done!

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.720
So this is taro simmered in broth.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:47.800
Next up, the mackerel pike!

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.470
When you're dealing with a whole fish,

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.770
make sure you run it under
water before you start preparing it.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:59.820
Once you've washed the sliminess
off the fish, dry them off thoroughly.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.240
To remove the odor, lightly salt the mackerel pike,

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.530
and then leave them for 10 to 15 minutes.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:09.280
This will draw out the moisture, so wipe it away.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.750
Lightly slit the mackerel pike's skin,

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:17.000
and salt them again, but this time,
for seasoning, and start grilling them.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.500
I have returned.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.250
So, you're in the midst of cooking.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.340
I could catch the aroma all the way in the—

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:26.720
What?

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:28.970
Welcome home!

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.470
Well, well, Saber...

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.640
I hope you don't mind my being here.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.310
What's Caster doing here?

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.900
Learning to cook from the boy.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.400
Do you really think I'd buy that?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.360
Well, it's true.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.400
I'm glad you're here. Would you mind tasting this?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.200
That's not laced with something, right?

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:53.660
It's all right, Saber. I guarantee it's safe.

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:16.520
I wonder if I can make Master Souichirou happy now!

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:20.520
I see.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.070
Um, okay, fine!

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:25.940
I'll be looking forward to the finished product!

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:27.360
Oh really?

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.870
Right. Okay, let's finish off the rest now, huh?

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:38.250
After boiling the mustard spinach, place it in ice water.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:39.370
Right.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:42.580
Then, remove the oil from the
deep-fried tofu you'll add to the spinach.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.460
Remove the oil?

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:46.550
Make sure you don't bring the miso soup to a boil.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.680
Because if you do, it'll lose its fragrance and flavor.

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:51.550
Wait, hold up a second, boy!

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:54.050
Could you go a little slower?

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:56.560
This isn't a high-speed chant, after all.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:58.560
Was that too much of an info dump?

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:02.230
Um, I'm gonna write down these instructions, okay?

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:04.900
All right!

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:09.400
Now we just arrange the food, and we're done!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.990
Thank you for the meal!

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.840
Delicious!

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.470
The taro... If we left them overnight,

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:34.930
the flavor would steep more,
and the taste would be even better.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:40.020
I-In that case, Shirou, we shouldn't finish it all, right?

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:44.060
Not only is the fish plump and soft,
the side dish is also delicious.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:46.520
You certainly are a skilled cook, boy.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.150
Thank you, boy.

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:54.070
I'm looking forward to cooking
this for Master Souichirou.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.080
No.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:09.420
I'm sure that I made this exactly
the way the boy taught me.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:12.800
But it's slightly off.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:17.180
B-But I'm sure there's nothing wrong with how it tastes.

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:19.350
Caster...

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.180
Master Souichirou!

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.480
I came to check on you, since you have yet to return.

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.900
Please forgive me.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:30.990
You see,

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:36.240
I wanted to make you a
delicious meal, Master Souichirou.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:44.500
But I seem to have been slightly unsuccessful.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.290
It's just not as easy as I thought.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:07.770
Caster...

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:12.070
If you feel that you've failed, just try again.

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.530
I'll keep you company as much as you need.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:19.780
Right.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.790
Thank you very much...

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.750
Master Souichirou.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:33.210
I shall do my best!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.350
Master Souichirou, let me bring this over to the table.
